      {
        "id": "p16-q84",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\log_x\\left(\\frac{1}{25}\\right)=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=5$",
          "worked": "A logarithmic base requires $x>0$ and $x\\ne1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^{-2}&=\\frac{1}{25}\\\\\\frac{1}{x^2}&=\\frac{1}{25}\\\\x^2&=25\\\\x&=\\pm5\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $x=-5$ because the base must be positive. Hence $x=5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q85",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\log_x(3)=\\frac{1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=9$",
          "worked": "A logarithmic base requires $x>0$ and $x\\ne1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^{1/2}&=3\\\\x&=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe base $9$ satisfies both restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
